# Taigam, Master Opportunist: Memnite is Bot1's second spell on turn three (after Mox Ruby), so flurry copies it: the copy becomes a token
# Memnite as it resolves (CR 707.10f) and the original is exiled with four time counters. At turn eleven's upkeep the last counter
# comes off, the original is cast for free and, as a creature cast by suspend, has haste (CR 702.62a): it attacks the turn it arrives, which the
# token (in play since turn three) could do anyway, so only the newer Memnite attacks and Bot2 takes exactly 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Taigam, Master Opportunist
Memnite
Mox Ruby
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

